Subject: [PATCH] HID: surface-hid: suspend HID clients before shutdown

The Surface HID transport forwards system-sleep callbacks to its HID
clients but lacks a shutdown callback. Invoke the existing HID suspend
routine before the SAM controller shuts down so touchpad reporting is
quiesced on poweroff too.

On an attached Surface Pro Flex Keyboard, a bounded reporting-switch test
stopped haptic clicking and restored it afterward. With this callback
loaded on 7.2.0-sp11-73wip3, the maintainer reports clicking stopped on
full shutdown and input returned on the subsequent boot. That boot used
the original on-disk module. Subsequent reported cold-boot failures may
have involved premature checks: a later captured shutdown confirmed
successful disable commands before SAM shutdown, and the maintainer
confirmed haptics were off after a 20-second settling window. This is not
a measured delay; actual cutoff latency and repeated reliability remain
unqualified. Battery savings and Bluetooth behavior are unmeasured.
A subsequent uninstrumented shutdown again left haptics active, so this
remains an unresolved/intermittent fix. The successful instrumented trace
does not establish ordinary shutdown reliability.

Normal operation and existing suspend/resume callbacks are unchanged.
---
diff --git a/drivers/hid/surface-hid/surface_hid.c b/drivers/hid/surface-hid/surface_hid.c
index eae47e0d95ed..5a341b2aeb01 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/surface-hid/surface_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/surface-hid/surface_hid.c
@@ -229,6 +229,18 @@ static void surface_hid_remove(struct ssam_device *sdev)
 	surface_hid_device_destroy(ssam_device_get_drvdata(sdev));
 }
 
+static void surface_hid_shutdown(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct surface_hid_device *shid = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	int status;
+
+	/* Put HID clients into their low-power mode before SAM shuts down. */
+	status = hid_driver_suspend(shid->hid, PMSG_SUSPEND);
+	if (status)
+		dev_warn(dev, "failed to suspend HID device for shutdown: %d\n",
+			 status);
+}
+
 static const struct ssam_device_id surface_hid_match[] = {
 	{ SSAM_SDEV(HID, ANY, SSAM_SSH_IID_ANY, 0x00) },
 	{ },
@@ -241,6 +253,7 @@ static struct ssam_device_driver surface_hid_driver = {
 	.match_table = surface_hid_match,
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "surface_hid",
+		.shutdown = surface_hid_shutdown,
 		.pm = &surface_hid_pm_ops,
 		.probe_type = PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
